<title>USA: Bay Apartment sells redeemable pfd stock.</title>
<headline>Bay Apartment sells redeemable pfd stock.</headline>
<dateline>SAN JOSE, Calif. 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bay Apartment Communities said it sold 2,300,000 shares of 8.5 percent Series C Cumulative Redeemable Preferred Stock at $25 per share.</p>
<p>Net proceeds from the offering, after all anticipated issuance costs, are estimated to be about $55.6 million.</p>
<p>The preferred stock, which may be redeemed by the company at $25 per share, plus accrued and unpaid dividends, on or after June 20, 2002 has no stated maturity, sinking fund or mandatory redemption and is not convertible into any other securities of the company.</p>
</text>
